-- **Generation:** `beforeRequest` (replace the messages of one request), `afterResponse`, `beforeRetry` (decide whether and when a failed request is tried again, instead of `settings.retry`), `onYield` (continue the run with another user message), `afterTools` (runs once a round's tools are done), and `afterRun` (tasks to run before the run ends, below).
+- **Generation:** `beforeRequest` (replace the messages of one request), `afterResponse`, `beforeRetry` (decide whether and when a failed request is tried again, instead of `settings.retry`), `onYield` (continue the run with another user message), `afterTools` (runs once a round's tools are done; `{ end: true }` ends the run there, as `terminate` from every call would), and `afterRun` (tasks to run before the run ends, below).
 - **Tools:** `beforeTool` (block or rewrite arguments) and `afterTool` (replace the result). `afterTool` sees every result a tool task writes, also the error results the Harness writes itself (unavailable, invalid, blocked, interrupted, restart limit, aborted), told apart by their diagnostic code; past `settings.restartLimit` it no longer runs. On an abort it runs inside the abort handler, so a slow hook delays `abort()`.
 
 To limit a hook to some conversations, select its extension only there, for example with `configure({ extensions: { add: [Guard] } })`.
